-- The mantissa PACKER, bound to SQL. The decoder has always been callable from
-- SQL; the builder was reachable only from managed code, so anything in SQL that
-- needed a trajectory -- a regress fixture, a repair, an ad-hoc probe -- had no way
-- to make one except to reimplement the packing, which would be a second
-- implementation of the identity encoding.
--
-- This calls trajectory_build() from engine/core, the same function the compose
-- path calls, so a trajectory produced here is byte-identical to one produced at
-- ingest. Same code, one more binding. The engine is already resident in the
-- backend, so it is a direct call into loaded memory.
--
-- IMMUTABLE: the packing is a pure function of the ordered ids.
CREATE OR REPLACE FUNCTION @extschema@.laplace_trajectory_build(ids bytea[])
    RETURNS geometry
    AS 'MODULE_PATHNAME', 'pg_laplace_trajectory_build'
    LANGUAGE C LAPLACE_IMMUTABLE_STRICT;
